data: {"text":"1. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in FIR No. 78/2026 dated 01.04.2026, registered at Police"}

data: {"text":" Station Lalpur, under Sections 303 and 351 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, and is"}

data: {"text":" presently languishing in judicial custody since 02.04.2026, without any justifiable cause.\n\n2. That"}

data: {"text":" the present case arises out of a property dispute between the Complainant and the Applicant's family. The Applicant subm"}

data: {"text":"its that he has been falsely implicated in the said FIR due to the ongoing civil dispute regarding"}

data: {"text":" the property, and the Complainant has misused the criminal law machinery to settle"}

data: {"text":" personal scores and to harass the Applicant and his family members.\n\n3. That the Applicant was not present at the spot at the time of the alleged incident and has been"}

data: {"text":" falsely implicated with malicious intent. The Applicant has CCTV evidence from a nearby shop which clearly establishes his presence elsewhere at the time when"}

data: {"text":" the alleged incident is said to have occurred. This electronic evidence conclusively proves that the Applicant could not have committed"}

data: {"text":" the alleged offence and that the allegations levelled against him are completely baseless and"}

data: {"text":" fabricated.\n\n4. That the Applicant was arrested on 02.04.2026 and has been in judicial custody since then. The investigation is pending and"}

data: {"text":" the Applicant has not been given an opportunity to present the exonerating evidence in"}

data: {"text":" his possession, including the CCTV footage that establishes his alibi.\n\n5. That the Applicant is"}

data: {"text":" a respectable member of society with deep roots in the community and has no previous criminal ant"}

data: {"text":"ecedents. He is not a person who would abscond or evade the process"}

data: {"text":" of law. The Applicant undertakes to cooperate fully with the investigation and to appear before the investigating agency as"}

data: {"text":" and when required.\n\n6. That there is no flight risk involved as the Applicant belongs to a respectable family and has permanent residence in the area. He"}

data: {"text":" has been cooperating with the investigation since the beginning and has never attempted to influence any witness or tam"}

data: {"text":"per with any evidence. The Applicant poses no threat to the society or to any witness"}

data: {"text":" in the case.\n\n7. That the continued detention of the Applicant in judicial custody is violative of his fundamental right to life and personal liberty as"}

data: {"text":" guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India. The Applicant has already suffered sufficient incarceration and his"}

data: {"text":" further detention would amount to pre-trial punishment.\n\n8. That while Section 303 of BNS is"}

data: {"text":" non-bailable and Section 351 of BNS is bailable, the facts and circumstances of the present case warrant the grant of bail to the Applicant. The allegations are"}

data: {"text":" completely false and fabricated, and there is credible evidence to support the Applicant's innocence in the form of CCTV footage establishing"}

data: {"text":" his presence elsewhere at the time of the alleged incident.\n\n9. That the Applicant undertakes to abide by all conditions that this"}

data: {"text":" Hon'ble Court may deem fit to impose while granting bail. He shall not leave the jurisdiction of this Hon"}

data: {"text":"'ble Court without prior permission, shall cooperate with the investigation, and shall not influence any witness or tamper with any evidence.\n\n10. That the Applic"}

data: {"text":"ant has not made any previous application for bail before any Court in connection"}

data: {"text":" with the present case, and this is the first application for regular bail being moved before this Hon'ble Court."}

